{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/809955-alternate-vitae-pool-idea-crazy-dumb-ill-thought-out","id":809955,"title":"Alternate Vitae Pool Idea [Crazy? Dumb? Ill-Thought Out?]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-15T17:45:12-08:00","id":809955,"title":"Alternate Vitae Pool Idea [Crazy? Dumb? Ill-Thought Out?]","content":"<b>Note:</b> These rules <i>solely</i> apply to Kindred. Ghouls work like they do normally.<br /> <br /> Under this schema, you have a Vitae pool of 10. That's it; your Blood Potency doesn't increase it <i>at all</i>.<br /> <br /> \u2022 There's no limit on how much Vitae you can spend at once. Blow your entire pool if you want!<br /> \u2022 When you take your daily &quot;nap&quot;, you lose Vitae in excess of your Blood Potency. So if you go to bed with 7 Vitae in your pool and only have Blood Potency 3, you lose all but 3 points before you wake up. In other words, you'd wake up with 2 Vitae (4 lost from falling asleep, 1 spent to wake up). This is referred to as Sleep Burn.<br /> \u2022 You may choose to spend Vitae as Sleep Burn in excess to the amount you lose due to getting some shut-eye.<br /> \u2022 You may heal one level of Aggravated damage for every 5 Vitae lost to Sleep Burn.<br /> \u2022 Revenants effectively have Blood Potency 0. They only wake up from Daysleep if someone feeds them blood or Vitae.<br /> <hr /><br /> Now, what does this change?<br /> <br /> \u2022 &quot;Young&quot; Kindred are going to <i>starving</i> and vulnerable when they wake up. Expect to start <i>every</i> night with a feeding scene.<br /> \u2022 As Kindred gain more Blood Potency, they have the <i>luxury</i> of being able to go longer without eating.<br /> \u2022 Herds and Feeding Grounds probably become all the more vital - an Elder letting you use one of their Feeding Grounds or giving you someone to chow on when you wake up is going to be one <i>hell</i> of a bargaining chip.<br /> \u2022 Personal power is going to be more about skill and less about having a huge Vitae Pool to toss around. A lot of &quot;Elder Devotions&quot; become accessible to the common Kindred.<br /> \u2022 Kindred with low Blood Potency have a <i>strong</i> incentive to run around and get things done before they essentially waste Vitae. If they have a Herd or a Feeding Ground, expect to see a lot of conspicuous spending.<br /> \u2022 Probably a bunch of other things! This hasn't been playtested yet (who am I kidding? <i>Nothing</i> I write is playtested!), so there's probably some really weird extra thing that pops up when you do this.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T18:53:16-08:00","id":810002,"title":"","content":"Letting you blow all your Vitae in a single round definitely has some unbalancing risks. If you can equal the expenditure of any Elder out there (who has the same blood pool and expenditure rate) then you'd better hope the Elder in question has other ways of defending themselves, because getting caught off guard by one bad tempered neonate who suddenly dumps 20 extra dice into that sudden attack may wreck their day (and if multiple people get involved and are spending it all at once, it's all but literally a bloodbath).<br /> <br /> Additionally, the Sleep Burn thing kind of conflicts with at least one bloodline, the Neglatu, who have this sort of issue as their bloodline Bane.<br /> <br /> Revenants in this scheme are also screwed; they don't even get a single chance to wake up, which means you have to basically keep them as blood-fed pets (and feed them a LOT if you want to keep them viable at all, which cuts into your own feeding if you have limited resources).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;There is the world of light, and the world of darkness. And some in the light prefer the darkness.&quot; \u2014 Loren Eiseley, <i>The Night Country</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/583-zsander","name":"Zsander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar583_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T19:54:23-08:00","id":810030,"title":"","content":"For your first point: what stops you from going up to the Queen of England and smacking her in the face? That's what Elders have got - their advantage is being <i>entrenched</i>. Part of the point of this was eliminating the divide between Elders and Neonates in that regard, so I consider that a success.<br /> <br /> Granted, that. Elder is going to have more dots in Disciplines and more Devotions than the Neonate as well, so they have <i>better</i> stuff to spend it on. And the whole fact that they're <i>vastly</i> more likely to win Clash of Wills, so if they have Auspex up and running...<br /> <br /> But yeah - flattening the setting. The main advantage that Elders have <i>here</i> is that they don't have to eat every night and that they are more likely to have Herds/Feeding Grounds/Retainers to cut down on the time they spend on that stuff.<br /> <br /> Never underestimate the advantages of not having to go out and hunt down your dinner <i>every single night</i>. And having the Vitae to do so when you do.<br /> <hr /><br /> The Neglatu's Bane is that they can't form Blood Bonds. Their <i>Gift</i> boosts the amount of Vitae that their Revenant &quot;family&quot; gets to keep - it pretty much works as-is.<br /> <br /> And Revenants being screwed is actually another aim of this - it makes the Neglatu scarier, for one, and I kinda want the whole &quot;keep 'em in cryogenic freezing without the stuff related to torpor&quot; aspect. Plus, you can <i>literally</i> just slaughter a rat over their mouth to give them the blood they need to wake up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T02:43:36-08:00","id":810152,"title":"","content":"You haven't so much screwed revenants there as completely eradicated them. The whole point is that they wake up starving each night an probably eat the first person they see in a frenzy. This just makes them a crappy sort of ghoul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T03:35:37-08:00","id":810163,"title":"","content":"As far as I can tell... I don't think this accomplished the intended goal of &quot;flattening&quot; the setting. Neonates have zero power now. This is now &quot;Vampire: the US Student Loan Crisis taken to 11.&quot; except instead of just endless debt, there's increased risk of murdering anyone you care about, death, and insanity.<br /> <br /> In the default, Neonates aren't entrenched, but have much greater flexibility for it. This makes them dangerous, because it's harder for the Elders to control them. And few vampires are so powerful, that they can realistically rely on their personal power to avoid getting offed in a rebellion if they're not careful with their powerful.<br /> <br /> With this... Neonates have jack-shit. They wake up with zero vitae until they hit BP 2. If they're lucky, they survive long enough to deal with their Humanity dropping like a rock, and the giant debt they've racked up to other vampires. Most will be killed after one too many frenzies. Or maybe locked up for some amount of time until their BP goes up. <br /> <br /> This doesn't really do much for evening the field. They're still going to be way behind with Attributes, Skills, Merits, Disciplines, and etc. &quot;I can drop 10 BP for +20 dice to attack!&quot; vs. &quot;I can drop 1 BP and use Celerity so you miss... and I still have 9 BP left to put you down.&quot; Not to mention that young vampires aren't really going to be able to maintain Ghouls easily, so Elders will come to most situations with personal power <i>and</i> numbers now.<br /> <br /> As is, I wouldn't want to play this. It's like Mage the Ascension, and pretty much needing to drop at least 1 into Avatar, and raise Arete to 2, or be insanely weak at start. There is pretty much zero reason to not drop Merit points on starting with BP 2 or 3 so you can actually expect to survive more than a couple sessions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T05:06:30-08:00","id":810178,"title":"","content":"I agree that it doesn't do much to level the playing field. A Neonate wakes up with 0-1 vitae, is starving and has to find a way to feed without proper access to their powers. An elder wakes up with 4-5, and walks over to their feeding ground for a quick snack at the nightclub before going and messing with some neonates getting beaten up by some tramps. Feeding grounds are going to be so important neonates are going to be either owned by an elder or struggling to get through the night, as the ones who can make it by without feeding grounds also have the time and people to grab and enforce feeding grounds while the neonates are getting enough blood to keep their beasts under control.<br /> <br /> If you also remove the beast it works, but that's an additional house rule not included.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T05:59:33-08:00","id":810199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/809955-alternate-vitae-pool-idea-crazy-dumb-ill-thought-out#post809955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2022 &quot;Young&quot; Kindred are going to <i>starving</i> and vulnerable when they wake up. Expect to start <i>every</i> night with a feeding scene.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well, the whole point of Location and Herd is being able to feed off screen. Feeding scenes get old after a while in game.<br /> <br /> I suspect that the players will simply raise up their BP and Herd right away to make it a non-issue. Because it gets old fast.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2022 As Kindred gain more Blood Potency, they have the <i>luxury</i> of being able to go longer without eating. </div> </div> </div> Its doubtful they would, however. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2022 Herds and Feeding Grounds probably become all the more vital - an Elder letting you use one of their Feeding Grounds or giving you someone to chow on when you wake up is going to be one <i>hell</i> of a bargaining chip. </div> </div> </div> You're going to have to rework the merits. Because, as things stand, you've completely destroyed what Feeding Grounds means - this merit affected your effective starting vitae, and you've reruled starting vitae to BP. Herd let you get vitae during the middle of the night.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2022 Personal power is going to be more about skill and less about having a huge Vitae Pool to toss around. A lot of &quot;Elder Devotions&quot; become accessible to the common Kindred. </div> </div> </div> Not entirely true. So many disciplines now need vitae to use. Weaker Kindred wont' be able to use Dominate 2 to help them feed, for instance. You made elder devotions accessable, but you limited the ability to use disciplines mutliple times each night. And elders are still going to be having the better benefits from frenzy, larger and better disciplines, better skills and attributes, and so on. <br /> <br /> Also, blowing all your vitae in an attack is actually an inefficient tactic. You're better off saving vitae for healing (average of negating 1 success/3 dice per vitae instead of getting 2 dice to an attack). Elders really haven't quite benefited from the larger dice pool. I mean, in theory, its there. Its nice. But its never been as critical as other things. BP is more important in 2e, but because of Predator's Aura and Frenzy bonuses, not your vitae capacity. If anything, with how Vigor and Resilience work now, spending vitae for+2 dice is LESS of an issue.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2022 Kindred with low Blood Potency have a <i>strong</i> incentive to run around and get things done before they essentially waste Vitae. If they have a Herd or a Feeding Ground, expect to see a lot of conspicuous spending. </div> </div> </div> Or they have a strong incentive to to do very little. Conserve energy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2022 Probably a bunch of other things! This hasn't been playtested yet (who am I kidding? <i>Nothing</i> I write is playtested!), so there's probably some really weird extra thing that pops up when you do this. </div> </div> </div> The biggest issue is the whole &quot;weak and feral young&quot; issue that others mentioned. I won't go more into it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T06:13:26-08:00","id":810201,"title":"","content":"Also Neonates under this scheme can heal Aggravated damage a lot faster than elders can. That's not right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T06:22:13-08:00","id":810204,"title":"","content":"And if they don't go to sleep or are awakened during the day, then what? Elders are the only ones most likely to make the initial roll to stay awake (and be effective) for any length of time in the first place.<br /> <br /> I don't see vampires purposely siring offspring. The liability a childe brings far exceeds any potential profit that can be gained just as effectively from ghouls or vinculumed humans. Maybe just human prodigies. The potential problem of accidental embrace via revenant is self correcting. The dead and buried don't rise unless they're dug up and fed vitae. Maybe once every 10th blue moon an unidentified dead guy may rise that night in the morgue or funeral home, slaughters the night shift, and just happens to diablerize his unsuspecting sire or other vampire and elevates himself in the process.<br /> <br /> The typical city is likely to be limited to one or two clans of vampires with a single progenitor. (Daeva and Nosferatu would be my guess. They are the only ones with massive unresistable crowd control powers and personal power disciplines.) Anything else is not only competition for food but they're a dangerous unknown element that will upset the status quo and jeopardize the Masquerade. Unacceptable in the face of every other supernatural having a much larger gas tank and personal powers that equal or exceed a vampire's.<br /> <br /> If covenants exist, its likely to be only the Carthians. They're the only ones capable of safeguarding their hunting grounds, having 2 or 3 for the price of one in social contacts and food sources, and the ability to mystically strike down anyone who violates their rules. Everyone else is a vitae black hole that never pays off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 01-16-2016, 09:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T09:42:57-08:00","id":810267,"title":"","content":"@MCN Worth noting that Feeding Grounds only modifies &quot;starting vitae&quot; when you otherwise don't know how much vitae you would have. That is, after time skips, not when you wake up for the night. Otherwise, it adds to hunting rolls. It would still be useful for both its standard uses.<br /> <br /> That said, I really, really don't like this, either. It does seem like it would be somewhat enhanced by making the Blood Beats optional rule mandatory, maybe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T09:48:08-08:00","id":810268,"title":"","content":"I love the assumption that low Vitae = beaten up by tramps. You know, ignoring the fact that you've probably frenzied due to hunger, ignore all that damage from them kicking you (unless tramps suddenly started kicking you with Lethal damage when I wasn't looking), and that <i>every</i> Discipline gives you some free power. You're better off than a bog-standard mortal, even without Vitae to spend.<br /> <br /> Eh, shrugging on this one. No real need for anyone else to post (unless they want to) - I get the picture.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T16:57:54-08:00","id":810400,"title":"","content":"The Nos like it!<br /> At least those with True Wyrm and deep warrens.<br /> I see some of the interesting points but it might need more tweaking or the other parts of the system may. Thislooks like it may work better with first edition than second.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}